  "goodToKnow": "Die Städtepartnerschaft is town twinning: Hamburg und Marseille, Berlin und Paris. After the Second World War, Franco-German twinnings were a key tool of reconciliation, and there are now over two thousand between the two countries. Signs at town entrances often list the Partnerstädte. They promote school exchanges and visits. Plural: die Städtepartnerschaften."
